The original body isn't visible, so this rewrite assumes `FieldBase::GetBitsValue64(offset, bits)` exists with unsigned-extraction semantics. It replaces the generic template path with a single extraction and a branch-free sign extension. Edge cases (`bits == 0`, `bits >= 64`) are guarded to return the raw extracted value. I haven't compiled or diffed this against `GetBitsSignedValueT`, so verify it against the corpus before relying on it.

```cpp
FIT_SINT64 FieldBase::GetBitsSignedValue64(const FIT_UINT16 offset, const FIT_UINT8 bits) const
{
    const FIT_UINT64 raw = GetBitsValue64(offset, bits);
    if (bits == 0 || bits >= 64)
    {
        return static_cast<FIT_SINT64>(raw);
    }
    const unsigned int shift = 64u - static_cast<unsigned int>(bits);
    return static_cast<FIT_SINT64>(raw << shift) >> shift;
}
```